      "content": "a plant, also called herba capillaris, maidenhair (Latham, Dictionary s.v. capillus, MED s.v. capillus veneris n.), a fern (often cultivated) with delicate, pale green, fan-shaped pinnules, which occurs in shady humid habitats in subtropical and warm temperate parts of the world and was formerly much used in medicine (OED s.v. s.v. maidenhair n.)"
